  "notes": "Lines numbered as in Audio/Dominick.json (1-64). Choruses: lead lines all six, the bracketed hee-haws by the outer pair (the donkeys), the first la-la line by the middle four and the second by everyone. Verses tell the story: verse 1 passes it tree to tree 1->6, verse 2 back 6->1, verse 3 between the trios. Final six hee-haws go round the choir one tree each. Looks (tools/fx.py, 23 Oct 2026): Italian tricolour running through, with rainbow sweeps; the resting trees watch whoever tells the story in the verses; spinning rainbow eyes on Buon Natale, rolling eyes on the hee-haws."
